fix(seeder-image): AddTorrent gRPC handler never sets result=true

gRPCService::AddTorrent (service.cpp) calls ezio::add_torrent and, on
success, falls through to `return Status::OK` without ever calling
`response->set_result(true)`. AddResponse.result is a proto3 bool, whose
zero value is false, so every successful AddTorrent call reports
result=false on the wire - indistinguishable from a real failure to any
client that checks it (as kezio's internal/seeder.Client.AddTorrent
does; a real failure still reaches the client as a distinct gRPC error
status via the existing catch block below, unaffected by this patch).
GetTorrentStatus immediately shows the torrent as added, proving the
underlying add_torrent() call itself succeeded; only the response's
result field was wrong.

Applied at Dockerfile.seeder build time (see EZIO_REF) against the
pinned upstream ezio revision, pending a matching fix upstream.

diff --git a/service.cpp b/service.cpp
index 437c355..7d1da82 100644
--- a/service.cpp
+++ b/service.cpp
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ Status gRPCService::AddTorrent(ServerContext *context,
 		return Status(grpc::StatusCode::UNAVAILABLE, e.what());
 	}
 
+	response->set_result(true);
 	return Status::OK;
 }
 
